# AI Agent Integration

## Context Bridge (`window.__ai__`)

Structured interface for AI agents (MCP servers, browser extensions, copilot sidepanels).

### Read context

```javascript
__ai__.context.getCurrentChat()
// { type: "stream", streamName: "general", topic: "bugs", messageCount: 42 }

__ai__.context.getCurrentUser()
// { userId: 1, email: "user@example.com", fullName: "John", realm: "https://..." }

__ai__.context.getAppState()
// { locale: "ru", theme: { palette: "orange-warm", mode: "dark" }, unreadCount: 15, online: true }

__ai__.context.getRecentMessages(10)
// [{ id, content, sender, timestamp }, ...]
```

### Subscribe to events

```javascript
__ai__.events.onNewMessage((msg) => {
  // { id: 123, content: "<p>Hello</p>", senderId: 42, timestamp: 1710000000 }
  // Use for: AI summarization, auto-reply, sentiment analysis
});

__ai__.events.onStateChange((state) => {
  // { locale, theme, unreadCount, online, runtime, version }
  // Use for: adaptive AI behavior
});
```

### Register commands

```javascript
const unsub = __ai__.commands.register({
  id: "summarize-chat",
  label: "Summarize chat",
  description: "Generate AI summary of current conversation",
  handler: async (args) => {
    const messages = __ai__.context.getRecentMessages(50);
    const summary = await callAI(messages);
    return summary;
  },
});

// Execute command
await __ai__.commands.execute("summarize-chat");

// List all registered commands
__ai__.commands.list();
```

## Use Cases

| Integration | How |
|-------------|-----|
| **Chat summarization** | `getRecentMessages()` → LLM → display summary |
| **Smart compose** | `getCurrentChat()` context → suggest reply |
| **Unread triage** | `getAppState().unreadCount` → prioritize channels |
| **Sentiment alert** | `onNewMessage()` → analyze → notify if negative |
| **Auto-translate** | `onNewMessage()` → detect language → translate |
| **Command palette** | `commands.register()` → user triggers via UI |
| **MCP server** | Read context → expose as MCP resources/tools |

## For AI Agent (code changes)

When adding new AI-relevant features:
1. Expose read-only state through `__ai__.context`
2. Notify `notifyAiNewMessage()` / `notifyAiStateChange()` from event handlers
3. Use `commands.register()` for AI-triggered actions
4. NEVER expose write access to stores directly — only through defined actions
5. Sanitize message content before exposing (it's HTML from Zulip)
